From 5cc2d4105f8318a327f50876ecf47208fc7da58e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 20:42:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] ACPI: SBS: Report full only when the battery is fully
 charged
To: "Rafael J. Wysocki" <rafael@kernel.org>,
    linux-acpi@vger.kernel.org
Cc: Len Brown <lenb@kernel.org>,
    Sebastian Reichel <sre@kernel.org>,
    linux-pm@vger.kernel.org,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

The driver reports a battery that neither charges nor discharges as
full. With a charge limit, the battery stops charging below full, and
user space then shows it as fully charged.

The battery reports FULLY_CHARGED in BatteryStatus, which the driver
already reads. Report full only when that bit is set and not charging
otherwise. On a MacBookPro15,1, BatteryStatus reads 0x00c0 while the
limit holds the battery at 90 percent, and the bit is set once the
battery is fully charged.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/acpi/sbs.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/sbs.c b/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
index 0939bb60b..0935fd776 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/sbs.c
@@ -42,6 +42,9 @@ module_param(cache_time, uint, 0644);
 MODULE_PARM_DESC(cache_time, "cache time in milliseconds");
 
 #define MAX_SBS_BAT			4
+
+/* BatteryStatus */
+#define ACPI_SBS_BATTERY_FULLY_CHARGED	BIT(5)
 #define ACPI_SBS_BLOCK_MAX		32
 
 static const struct acpi_device_id sbs_device_ids[] = {
@@ -170,8 +173,10 @@ static int acpi_sbs_battery_get_property(struct power_supply *psy,
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_DISCHARGING;
 		else if (battery->rate_now > 0)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING;
-		else
+		else if (battery->state & ACPI_SBS_BATTERY_FULLY_CHARGED)
 			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_FULL;
+		else
+			val->intval = POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_NOT_CHARGING;
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_PRESENT:
 		val->intval = battery->present;
-- 
